 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445216 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445216 1083 #uuid "c9e7ce1b-ea58-5c77-a5f2-354c10202f64" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445217 1080 "II and III only" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445217 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445217 1083 #uuid "d02e0e83-d95c-5ac9-a67d-e710736e75a3" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445218 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445218 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445218 1083 #uuid "e17bf533-f3b3-5889-bc5d-63042f883173" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445219 1080 "I only" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445219 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445219 1083 #uuid "ffe77668-6986-532b-ad24-452a980f2a61" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445209 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445211 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445212 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445214 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445217 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1077 "selection" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1078 #edb/ref 17592186445217 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445220 1079 #uuid "5e68d1f8-4799-5165-aca8-846dbe8edad9" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445205 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445206 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445207 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445210 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445219 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1077 "selection" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1078 #edb/ref 17592186445206 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445221 1079 #uuid "8da06cc9-b0c5-52b6-84dd-18ec2eed5c30" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445208 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445213 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445215 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445216 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445218 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1077 "selection" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1078 #edb/ref 17592186445215 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445222 1079 #uuid "df160bc6-de12-5b0e-ab4a-f86e448d27ab" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445223 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445220 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445223 1069 "q-94645" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445223 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445223 1071 "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. ${I}_{2}\\in R$\n\nII. For every $A,B\\in R,$ we have $A+B\\in R.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under addition." 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445223 1072 #uuid "110b21f6-4be1-556e-b1d2-7f471afa85fc" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445223 1074 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $R$ contains only matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers. However, ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is *not* a matrix of this form. So, ${I}_{2}\\notin R.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\in R$ and $B=[\\begin{aligned}c & d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\in R,$ where $a,b,c,d$ are real numbers. Then, \n\n$$\nA+B=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c & d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+c & b+d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $(a+c)$ and $(b+d)$ are real numbers, we conclude that $[\\begin{aligned}a+c & b+d \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\in R,$ i.e. $A+B\\in R.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set is closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445224 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445222 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445224 1069 "q-127876" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445224 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445224 1071 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,3⟩=17.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445224 1072 #uuid "685229d2-34f8-5173-a67b-785ec23ea6ca" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445224 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,3⟩=17$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,2{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445225 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445221 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445225 1069 "q-79834" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445225 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445225 1071 "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{-3x}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+9y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\nI. $y(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}$\n\nII. $y(x)=x{e}^{1-3x}$\n\nIII. $y(x)=\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}$" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445225 1072 #uuid "ad9f5224-cb10-5d73-824c-c4a1c6b129db" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445225 1074 "According to the superposition principle, if the function ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and $c$ is a constant, then $y(x)=c{y}_{1}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}=x\\cdot x{e}^{-3x}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\n- The function $y(x)=x{e}^{1-3x}=e\\cdot x{e}^{-3x}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=e.$\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445226 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445230 13194139534944 17592186045417 true] [17592186445226 1062 #uuid "02bcbecd-c304